text:
@frankandrews4470 I have been in both cars and the Byd have a cheaper plastic feeling.
Look at this test and see what they think. 
https://youtu.be/y-f9mLCxgrw?si=Rg6lR3Gc_qzWB5_b

@brettrun8575 if you think everything with 4 wheels looks like a tesla .. sure
the seal looks like a nice care, the model 3 just looks wrong
i prefere the ET5 touring, but my 220d shooting brake will last a few more years

@ninjarrow07  Indeed!
9-3, the same way a professional racing car driver would hold his/her hands, is the optimal way for controlling your car, which also happens to be the best way to do when using Teslas indicators.
Works great for me.

@Paul-ow9dd Just checked, and I can't find any market where it is rated at 1500kg.
in the USA it is rated to 750kg (braked) and in the EU it hasn't been rated for towing. This seems to be quite common for BYD in Europe. They clearly do't seem to care whether EU models can tow, so they don't rate them.
That is not good for me, so the Seal is out of the running, even if they did produce a hatched version. That. is a pity, because BYD is one of the companies that I would like to support.

@davidtolson7680 Model 3 is USA and China.

Model Y in Germany, USA and China.

All locations 100% owned by Tesla. BYD is partly owned by China.

@Alberto-mq7gw I agree, most reviews seem to have the BYD getting a reasonable chunk more range than the Tesla (say 15% more). But I don't think it really matters a huge amount for most people because the Tesla is still so much easier and faster to charge.

We know that most people drive less than 50 miles a day, so for those people longe range isn't a concern for daily use and when it is a concern it's for long trips - where the Tesla is still choice because of the charging situation.

For a few people, who perhaps regularly drive from home to a destination 280+ miles away and can charge at that destination, then the BYD might be a better choice because the range will be longer

@patmanrick Seal has ventilated seats as standard, a linear charge curve etc…

Literally half the features you boasted Tesla have hardly get used - so when you actually get down to it, they’re irrelevant.

Efficiency means nothing when the seal can go for longer anyway

@123silentassassin so wait, the software, luggage space, one pedal driving, charging network never get used?! The £6k cheaper isn't relevant? The efficiency, which makes it cheaper to run (as does access to supercharger network, because superchargers cost in the region of 40p per kWh vs up to 80p or more on other fast charge networks). 

It's actually the range which, in the absence of reliable fast charging infrastructure, matters less. The difference between a car that does 250 miles and one that does 280 miles is nothing day to day because most people drive fewer than 50 miles daily, and when it comes to longer trips charging becomes more important than absolute range most of the time (not all the time, but mostly - go and watch the out of spec roadtrips with the Lucid Air, which has a massive range but doesn't road trip well vs something like a Porsche Taycan which has much worse range but fast charging or vs Model S with worse range but faster and more reliable charging)

Also the Tesla software that isn't available on the BYD may not matter to you personally, in which case don't prioritise it 🤷🏽‍♂️ but for me, the ability to use dog mode, watch Netflix on the screen, mute rear chimes when baby is sleeping, quality and reliability of the routing software and sentry mode (was crucial for an insurance claim) add a lot of value and whilst I wouldn't necessarily say that they are necessary (realistically most things aren't) I would miss them quite a bit if I didn't have them. Perhaps without kids I'd care less, spend much more time in the car than I used to these days

@mconnah1 You can simulate indicators on most modern cars because they have buttons on the steering wheel. The "Have you tried it" isn't a worthy reply.
I simply do not understand why stalks are a bad idea. There's wipers, cruise control, lights, etc. on the stalks too.
I can understand it fits in with the minimalist look, but this is a step too far and will hinder sales, not promote them.

@no925 No, it's not right, can't you tell I'm upset!? I'm done with you, never acknowledging my feelings!
Go and do your 9 to 5, it's all you care about!
And you even edit your reply, how dare you!
